    <string name="help_start_end_q">What happens at the start and end?</string>
    <string name="help_start_end_a">Airplane mode turns on at the start. At the end, the app only undoes what it changed, so if airplane mode was already on, it stays on, and if you turned it off midway, it stays off.</string>
    <string name="help_wifi_q">How do the Wi-Fi options work?</string>
    <string name="help_wifi_a">“Turn off Wi-Fi at start” turns Wi-Fi off before airplane mode. “Turn on Wi-Fi at end” turns it back on, but only if the app turned it off.</string>
    <string name="help_overnight_q">Which day does an overnight schedule belong to?</string>
    <!-- %1$s is 11 PM and %2$s is 7 AM. -->
    <string name="help_overnight_a">The day it starts. A Friday schedule from %1$s to %2$s ends on Saturday morning.</string>
    <string name="help_once_q">What does a schedule without days do?</string>
    <string name="help_once_a">It runs once at its next start time, then switches itself off. If you switch it on between its start and end, it starts right away.</string>
    <string name="help_change_active_q">What happens if I change an active schedule?</string>
    <string name="help_change_active_a">Switching a schedule off or deleting it ends it right away, like a normal end. Switching on or adding a schedule that covers the current time starts it right away. Editing the times starts or ends it to match.</string>
    <string name="help_missed_q">Why didn\'t airplane mode turn on or off?</string>
    <string name="help_missed_a">Shizuku wasn\'t running at that time. The app doesn\'t automatically catch up by design.</string>
    <string name="help_shizuku_stopped_q">Why did Shizuku stop?</string>
    <string name="help_shizuku_stopped_a">You may need to start Shizuku again whenever the phone restarts. Turn on “Remind me if Shizuku is off” in Settings to get a warning an hour before a schedule runs.</string>
    <string name="help_overlap_q">Why can\'t two schedules overlap?</string>
    <string name="help_overlap_a">Only one schedule can be in charge at a time, so switched-on schedules can\'t overlap. Back-to-back schedules behave as merged, and airplane mode stays on in between. Wi-Fi follows the first one\'s start option and the last one\'s end option.</string>

